<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 3.02 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 3.02 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0735 to the dollar, up from 3.0745 on Monday and at 1.8255 to the mark, down from 1.8225, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.02 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Monday's 2.96 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
